Here is the commit message:
LUCENE-7698: fix CommonGramsQueryFilter to not produce a
 disconnected token graph

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the `CommonGramsQueryFilter` producing a disconnected token graph due to not properly setting the position length of tokens back to 1 when they are of gram type. This disconnection interfered with the correct parsing and execution of phrase queries, leading to unexpected behavior in query results.

Here is the patch:
 import org.apache.lucene.analysis.TokenFilter;
 import org.apache.lucene.analysis.tokenattributes.PositionIncrementAttribute;
+import org.apache.lucene.analysis.tokenattributes.PositionLengthAttribute;
